1.0beta6

* Fix sinh_rd, sinh_ru and sinh_rz at x = +-710.475860073944, where
  they returned +-inf instead of +-the largest double.
* Fix atanpi_rd, atanpi_ru and atanpi_rz for finite |x| >= 2^54, where
  they returned +-1/2.
* Fix atanpi_ru(1) and atanpi_rd(-1), which returned the double next
  to +-1/4 instead of +-1/4.
* Stop counting calls to the accurate step in a global variable, which
  was not safe when several threads call crlibm.
* Fix asin, acos, asinpi and acospi for |x| >= 0.75, where they could
  round to the wrong neighbour, and the directed modes could return a
  value on the wrong side of the exact result.
* Fix asinpi_rd and asinpi_ru for negative x, where they could round
  toward zero instead of down or up.
* Fix sinpi and tanpi for 2^-1000 <= |x| < 2^-950, where they could
  round to the wrong neighbour, and the directed modes could return a
  value on the wrong side of the exact result.
* Use the portable log by default. --enable-double-extended builds
  log-de.c as before.
* Compile with -ffp-contract=off.
* Fix the build of crlibm_exit without fpu_control.h.
